	(gr_text "PLEASE READ and keep in mind:\n\n- Please do not change the board dimensions or the 4 corner screws\n  as they are what I'm designing a lot of structural stuff around.\n- 4 layer: SIGNAL, GROUND, GROUND, SIGNAL\n- Do not route any traces AT ALL on the inner two layers\n- They must remain as unimpeaded ground planes.\n- The two signal (outer) layers have ground fill.\n- No components on back of board please\n\n- Keep analog and digital traces and components physically\n  away from each other (have an analog side and a digital side)\n- Route I2C first (since they are high speed) to give them clean paths\n- Keep I2C paths as short as possible\n- Then route the power\n- The 100nF capacitors at each VDD pin MUST be physically very close to\n  the VDD pin of the chip.\n- Put a ground via (Press V, make sure net is GND) next to every GND pad\n- The 470 ohm resistors at each output should be physically close to\n  its output pin.\n- Use 0.2mm wide traces. (except for power, probably 0.3mm for power)\n- Don't worry if the small components silkscreen labels get overlapped.\n\n- If you select whole areas on the schematic then switch to PCB mode,\n  the PCB footprints of the components in your selection will be selected\n  (helps speed up the component placement)\n\nThank you!! <33"
		(at 53.6 195.1 0)
		(layer "User.1")
		(uuid "69e5ec43-203c-41bf-9ba5-0cbf7650ba59")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(thickness 0.3)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
	)
	(gr_text "analog"
		(at 91.7 67.7 0)
		(layer "User.1")
		(uuid "9643f98d-5316-4970-9a66-5487c886b734")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(thickness 0.3)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
	)
	(gr_text "digital"
		(at 91.8 73.2 0)
